# Drop-in for apt-daily-upgrade.timer (moodle-server-care, skills/maintenance; references/unattended-upgrades.md).
# Target: /etc/systemd/system/apt-daily-upgrade.timer.d/override.conf (what `systemctl edit apt-daily-upgrade.timer` writes).
# Why: unattended-upgrades restarts services it upgrades (the DB server, nginx, Redis, PHP-FPM if its origin is
# allowed). The distribution default (06:00 + up to 60 min on Debian) is often a busy hour. Move it into the measured
# quiet window, AFTER the nightly backup's hard stop, so an upgrade never restarts the DB under a running dump.
# OnCalendar is server local time. The empty OnCalendar= line clears the packaged schedule first.
# Rollback: systemctl revert apt-daily-upgrade.timer && systemctl daemon-reload
[Timer]
OnCalendar=
OnCalendar=*-*-* @APT_AT@
RandomizedDelaySec=@APT_DELAY@
